msgid "Choose which of the WooCommerce Admin features should be disabled. The ones you choose will be <strong>disabled</strong>, and the ones that had not been selected will stay <strong>active</strong>.<br />This list comes from WooCommerce itself. Since WooCommerce 11, WooCommerce only lets plugins switch off a few of its admin features this way (often just Store alerts), so the list may be short. WooCommerce Analytics can be turned off under WooCommerce > Settings > Advanced > Features, and the Marketing hub with the Marketing Hub option below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings/class-disable-bloat-settings-main.php:595
msgid "Disable Marketing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings/class-disable-bloat-settings-main.php:596
msgid "This option will completely disable WooCommerce Marketing Hub. Coupon menu entry will stay accessible the old way (WooCommerce -> Coupons)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings/class-disable-bloat-settings-main.php:603
msgid "WooCommerce is constantly trying to promote and advertise add-ons by adding nags to your admin panel. Now you can turn off or hide them."
